Hard constraints:
1. Do not use emoji as core production UI icons. Use the PUTDUK SVG system.
2. Do not let the client determine mining, settlement, ledger or balance values.
3. Use server time for trial/mining/event/rule calculations.
4. Do not write mining progress every second.
5. Trial ledger and real wallet ledger are separate.
6. Asset mutations must be ledger-first and idempotent.
7. Economic rules are versioned with effective timestamps.
8. AI cannot directly mutate balances, approve funding/withdrawals or determine mining rewards.
9. User-facing UI is Korean-first and must remain simple enough for broad age ranges.
10. Premium quality is required: polished loading/empty/error states, responsive behavior, accessibility and restrained motion.
11. New features must identify their owning domain, audit impact, analytics impact and admin controls before implementation.
12. PUTDUK START may convert once to real withdrawable KRW after qualification,
    with a launch hard ceiling of KRW 5,000; funding is never a prerequisite.
13. The normal first-funding promotion is capped at KRW 10,000. A separately
    approved special operator campaign may exceed it only through explicit
    versioned cap and budget configuration.
14. Authoritative money uses balanced ledger transactions and entries; wallet
    balances are projections. Never use floating point.
15. Every post-commit notification/analytics/reward workflow starts from a
    versioned transactional outbox event.
16. Referral invitations are unlimited; standard automatic payout is at most
    KRW 10,000 per normally qualified referral, default split 5,000/5,000.
17. Shared IP alone is never automatic referral rejection or permanent block.
18. Mining products come from a versioned operator-approved catalog, never a
